WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.499
Redis runs one command at a time, on one thread.

2
00:00:06.499 --> 00:00:09.903
A prepaid card, balance:7, holds 100 euros.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.830
Two pods authorize it at once: 30 euros for coffee, 50 for fuel.

4
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.156
Each one reads the balance, and both see 100.

5
00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:21.356
Pod A writes 70, then pod B writes 50.

6
00:00:21.356 --> 00:00:25.173
The card paid 80 euros, and the balance says 50.

7
00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:32.648
Each command ran alone, but between two commands the thread serves everyone else, and that's where the other write landed.

8
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:36.113
MULTI and EXEC send a batch that runs as one step.

9
00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:40.377
But a batch can't read a value and decide, so WATCH adds a check.

10
00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:46.696
Pod A watches the balance, reads 100, and decides in its own code that 30 fits.

11
00:00:46.867 --> 00:00:49.529
Meanwhile pod B's payment writes 50.

12
00:00:49.529 --> 00:00:53.152
Pod A queues its new balance, 70, and sends EXEC.

13
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:58.161
The watched key changed after WATCH, so EXEC runs nothing and answers nil.

14
00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:02.726
Pod A starts over: it watches, reads 50, and writes 20.

15
00:01:02.726 --> 00:01:04.311
This time EXEC runs.

16
00:01:04.311 --> 00:01:05.896
Both payments count.

17
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.139
A Lua script removes the retry.

18
00:01:08.139 --> 00:01:13.300
Its read, test and write run as one command, so nothing can land in between.

19
00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.011
One command runs alone.

20
00:01:15.011 --> 00:01:20.115
Send the decision as one script, or WATCH the key and retry when EXEC fails.
